Rewritten: the part a Nodecode home can use without Hermes's credential pool.
The two provider adapters are the same reads the original makes -- Anthropic's
OAuth usage endpoint with the Claude Code client headers it uses so the
endpoint does not rate-limit a bare client, and the Codex usage endpoint with
the ChatGPT account id read out of the token -- and the same wake request,
one token of one model, sent to the same vendor. From the original's command
surface: `usage`/`report` (every account's windows), `balance` (which account
has the most headroom: `best`), `park`/`unpark` (kept in a text file instead
of Hermes's pool), and `wake`.

Left out, because each is Hermes's own runtime or store: `hermes auth add`
and its email verification (here an account is a line in the section and a
token in an environment variable), the credential pool itself and the
rotation strategy a Hermes session follows, the post-request hook that counts
tokens per account, bot and session, the weekly park schedules, the
five-minute balance timer, alerts and the daily summary through Hermes's send
channel, and the Hermes Desktop Accounts page and its dashboard API. The
weekly and forecast arithmetic the original derives from a timer has no
history here, so the report states the windows the vendor reports and nothing
projected.
